# SRG-APP-000845-AU-000320  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must for password-based authentication, verify when
# users create or update passwords, that the passwords are not found on the
# list of commonly-used, expected, or compromised passwords in IA-5 (1) (a).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000845-AU-000320
group:           V-263577
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004061
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk cannot screen a new password against a deny list, but it can refuse
                 a password at the moment it is created or updated: the benchmark
                 authority's implementation for this product (SPLK-CL-000410) is password
                 history, so authentication.conf [splunk_auth] enablePasswordHistory makes
                 the platform keep previously used passwords and passwordHistoryCount sets
                 how many it refuses to accept again. The composition rules also observed
                 on this requirement are asserted under SRG-APP-000870, where the product
                 STIG sets their values.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] enablePasswordHistory in true|True|TRUE|t|1|yes
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] passwordHistoryCount min 5
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] enablePasswordHistory https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] passwordHistoryCount https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Screening a new password against a list of commonly used, expected, or
                 compromised passwords - not offered by the product; carried by the
                 directory service or identity provider, and by the organization's policy
                 that maintains the list (see SRG-APP-000830).
external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, [splunk_auth] governs native
                 accounts only and the verification at password change happens at the
                 directory service or identity provider.
external:        Checking a new password against a list of commonly used, expected or
                 compromised passwords, which Splunk has no setting for: the native
                 controls cover reuse through enablePasswordHistory and
                 passwordHistoryCount, not membership of an external list.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:437 ([splunk_auth]), :554
                 (enablePasswordHistory, default false), :561 (passwordHistoryCount, 1-128,
                 default 24); SPLK-CL-000410 check and fix text
finding:         The application does not refuse a password at creation or update as the
                 product STIG requires - authentication.conf [splunk_auth]
                 enablePasswordHistory is missing or false, or passwordHistoryCount is 4 or
                 less - so a previously used password can be reinstated; this determination
                 is from the perspective of the application layer alone, screening against
                 a deny list of commonly used or compromised passwords being carried by the
                 identity provider and the organization's policy.
